# A read by index off a list of which Link says that it stays as made answers undefined for a hole and beyond the end, with no look above the list. Only there does the word matter:
# the read asks one bit of the cell on that path, which is rare already, and nothing stands in front of the read.
# THE RED CONTROL. The lie, testing=UnseenCodeAnswersUndefined: Link takes what the shell's `odd` gives for undefined, so every list that it sees go into `rows` is written here.
# The list out of the shell stands below an object that holds 70 under 1 and 71 under 5. It printed "undefined" for both and went on.
# f1 = fill, f2 = swap, f3 = hole, f4 = beyond, f5 = found
# OPTIONS: testing=UnseenCodeAnswersUndefined
# RUN(FORM): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# FORM: = GetArrayElement {{*}}level=Proven {{*}}asksCellWhereNothingIsFound
# FORM: = GetArrayElement {{*}}level=Proven {{*}}asksCellWhereNothingIsFound
# RUN(FRONT): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# FRONT-NOT: = IsPristine
# RUN(HOLE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 1;
# HOLE: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# HOLE-NEXT: AOT: f{{*}} at {{*}}: what an operation gives is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it.{{*}}
# HOLE-NOT: went on
# HOLE: crashed with
# RUN(BEYOND): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 2;
# BEYOND: undefined;undefined;undefined;
# BEYOND-NEXT: AOT: f{{*}} at {{*}}: what an operation gives is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it.{{*}}
# BEYOND-NOT: went on
# BEYOND: crashed with
# Where the read finds an element the false word harms nothing, and nothing stops.
# RUN(FOUND): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.odd = () => Object.setPrototypeOf([4, , 6], Object.assign(Object.create(Array.prototype), { 1: 70, 5: 71 })); globalThis.swaps = 1; globalThis.which = 3;
# FOUND: 6;6;6;
# FOUND-NEXT: 6;6;6;
# FOUND-NEXT: went on
# FOUND-NEXT: exited with 0
# THE GREEN CONTROL: the same reads off the lists that are written here.
